Keep a window in place when its new stacking sibling is unknown.

add_win drops windows destroyed before their attributes are read, such as
the window Chromium creates and destroys on every X11 drag motion. Restacking
the drag image above that unknown window used to move it to the bottom of the
paint list, hiding it until the next motion.

--- a/fastcompmgr.c
+++ b/fastcompmgr.c
@@ -1775,6 +1775,9 @@
   if (old_above != new_above) {
     win **prev;
 
+    if (new_above != None && !find_win(new_above))
+      return;
+
     /* unhook */
     for (prev = &list; *prev; prev = &(*prev)->next) {
       if ((*prev) == w) break;
